 "briefing": "# Infosys Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nThe research could not confirm any change at Infosys in the 16 October to 15 November 2026 window. Every search returned the same error (\"No valid search results found\"), so no news, launches, hires, or deals from this period were verified with a source. This briefing therefore records the gaps rather than listing unverified items. Before 17 November, the primary sources listed below should be checked directly.\n\n## News\n\nNo news items from the window were verified. This covers quarterly results, guidance, dividends, buybacks, board decisions, regulatory matters, legal proceedings, leadership commentary, analyst ratings, major share price moves, and workforce policy. The absence of results reflects a search failure, not confirmed absence of news.\n\n## Product and Service Launches\n\nNo product, platform, service, or AI offering launches dated within the window were identified. Searches covering Infosys's named AI and cloud platforms, press releases, and trade media did not return results. Whether any offering is new or an update to an existing one remains unassessed.\n\n## Executive and Talent Hires\n\nNo executive appointments, resignations, board changes, or key managerial personnel changes were confirmed. Headcount and hiring-related searches also returned no results, so workforce figures for the period are unknown.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo partnerships, acquisitions, divestitures, client contracts, large deal wins, or strategic investments were confirmed for the window. Any deal activity in this period is unknown until verified against primary sources.\n\n## Research Limitations\n\n- All search calls failed with the same error across varied query wording, which suggests a tool outage rather than a query problem.\n- No fetch of primary documents was completed, so filings and press releases were not reviewed.\n- No claims in this briefing rest on a retrieved source. Any item added later should be confirmed against the sources below before it is used in the meeting.\n\n## Where to Verify Before the Meeting\n\nEach of the following is a primary source to check for the 16 October to 15 November 2026 window. Listing them does not confirm any change.\n\n- [Infosys Newsroom](https://www.infosys.com/newsroom) for press releases and announcements\n- [Infosys Investors](https://www.infosys.com/investors) for results, filings, and investor announcements\n- [SEC EDGAR](https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/) for Infosys Form 6-K filings\n- [NSE India](https://www.nseindia.com) for corporate announcements under the INFY symbol\n- [BSE India](https://www.bseindia.com) for corporate announcements under scrip code 500209\n\n## Three Open Questions for Infosys\n\n1. Which developments from mid-October to mid-November 2026 has Infosys disclosed through exchange or SEC filings, and can you point us to them?\n2. Have there been any changes to senior leadership or key managerial personnel in the past month, and how were they disclosed?\n3. Are there any product launches, partnerships, or client contracts announced or planned for the coming months that we should be aware of?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Infosys Newsroom: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom\n[2] Infosys Investors: https://www.infosys.com/investors\n[3] SEC EDGAR: https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/\n[4] NSE India: https://www.nseindia.com\n[5] BSE India: https://www.bseindia.com",
